  m_Name: Carta_HortasComunitarias
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: "Hortas Comunit\xE1rias"
  _titleEn: Community Gardens
  _category: 0
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "Moradores transformam terrenos vazios em hortas e dividem a colheita:
    mais verde, comida fresca perto de casa e vizinhan\xE7a reunida."
  _summaryEn: 'Residents turn vacant lots into gardens and share the harvest: more
    green space, fresh food close to home and neighbors working together.'
  _realWorld: "Ros\xE1rio, na Argentina, lan\xE7ou em 2002, depois da crise de 2001,
    um programa municipal que transforma terrenos vazios em hortas ecol\xF3gicas
    de fam\xEDlias pobres, que vendem a colheita em feiras."
  _realWorldEn: After the 2001 crisis, Rosario, Argentina, launched a city program
    in 2002 that turns vacant lots into organic gardens run by low-income families,
    who sell the harvest at farmers' markets.
  _tradeOffs: 'Hortas precisam de gente que cuide delas toda semana e de terreno
    garantido: quando o dono do lote ou a prefeitura muda de ideia, a horta some.'
  _tradeOffsEn: 'Gardens need people to tend them every week and secure land: when
    the lot owner or the city changes its mind, the garden disappears.'
  _sources:
  - Label: "UCLG, Agricultura urbana e inclusi\xF3n social, Rosario"
    Url: https://www.uclg-cisdp.org/sites/default/files/observatory/files/2021-06/Rosario_ES.pdf
